<title>RUSSIA: Russian February inflation 1.5 pct vs 2.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian February inflation 1.5 pct vs 2.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's monthly consumer price inflation slowed in February to 1.5 percent, the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN CONSUMER PRICES    FEB 97    JAN 97    FEB 96</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	 +1.5	+2.3	+2.8</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	    N/A     +19.7     +89.0</p>
<p>Prices have risen 3.8 percent so far this year. The government is targeting annual inflation of about 12 percent. Seasonal factors typically push up inflation in January.</p>
<p>Average daily inflation slowed to 0.052 percent in February from 0.073 percent in January, the committee said.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
